{"connection_id": "BC-94f231981e34557fef57", "ref": "Didache 1.1", "target": "sec18", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "motif", "basis": "two ways, life and death", "note": "The commentary divides hearers between a destructive fate and purification with prayer; the Didache opens by distinguishing a way of life from a way of death, giving an early Christian ethical frame for the divided response."}
{"connection_id": "BC-6cbb2fc10593675f202d", "ref": "Gregory of Nyssa, Life of Moses II.20–21", "target": "sec18", "tradition": "incil", "kind": "yorum_gelenegi", "basis": "The unconsumed bush in Christian typology", "note": "In the burning-bush interpretation commonly placed in these sections, Gregory reads the bush's non-consumption through later Christian typology; the section numbering should be checked, but it is a concrete reception of the fire detail central to the commentary."}
